# Story: four windows arranged, one of them goes into the Dock, and a window is walked to the right. On its way it comes to lie in a row that
# shows, inside a column that does not: to the eye all is one row. Taking it out of that row alone would leave everybody left of whom
# they were and resize all three, under a "moved": the step nobody can see, in another coat. The press goes on until something shows: out of
# the row and past its neighbor. Where nothing lies beyond it says that it is at the edge, and no size changes.
# A press that changes nothing in the order a person sees is no step.
# Reference: IDEAS I21.
quiet
open Mail
open Notes
open Music
open Safari
arrange
minimize 103
focus 101
press dock right
expect ok
press dock right
expect ok
# To the eye: Notes, Safari, Mail, the Desktop.
expect left-of 102 104
expect left-of 104 101

# One press, and Mail is past the Desktop: at the right end.
press dock right
expect ok
expect moved-once
expect left-of 102 104
expect left-of 104 101
layout --ids
expect replied Desktop:0.6 | 101

# There is nowhere further: it says so, and nothing is resized.
press dock right
expect fail
expect said already at the right edge
expect still

# The same row with nothing beyond it, the Desktop being at the other end.
layout Desktop | 102 | (103 / (104 | 101)):2
focus 101
press dock right
expect fail
expect said already at the right edge
expect still
